WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
Good to have you on fascinating frontiers, episode 72.

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:05.940
Today is May 17th, 2026.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.900
Here's what's been unfolding in space and science

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:09.840
over the past week.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.860
Looking back at the stories from May 11 through today,

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.080
a handful stood out for what they reveal

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.620
about stellar behavior, planetary protection,

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.900
and how we keep extending our reach,

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.500
both robotic and human.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.840
Astronomers have identified ZTFJ007 plus 4804.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.260
As the first known hot sub-dorf plus white dwarf system

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.780
that produces dwarf nova outbursts.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:39.740
Observations from this wiki transient facility

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.060
combined with data from TESS

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:44.500
reveal the unexpected brightening events

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:45.900
in this rare binary.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:50.000
The discovery provides new insight into how such systems evolve

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.020
and how transient outbursts occur in compact stellar pairs,

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:56.500
essentially offering a fresh window

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.360
into the late stages of binary star life cycles.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:03.300
From rare stellar outbursts to practical efforts

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.340
protecting Earth from much closer celestial objects,

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.140
we turn next to planetary defense hardware.

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:13.520
Engineers continue design work on a new, near-earth asteroid

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:16.540
survey instrument intended to improve detection

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:17.720
of smaller objects.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.560
The telescope is expected to deliver earlier warnings

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.180
than current survey systems

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:26.320
by capturing fainter targets at greater distances.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.580
One more step towards shrinking the window of surprise

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:32.120
for objects we'd rather spot well in advance.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.480
While we refine our view of nearby threats,

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:38.740
engineers on another continent are stressed testing hardware

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:39.720
bound for Mars.

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:43.920
Full-scale structural test models of the Exo Mars rover

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.680
and its carrier spacecraft have now been completed.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:50.200
These replicas will undergo vibration, thermal,

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.220
and mechanical load tests to validate the design

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:55.520
without risking actual flight hardware.

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:58.980
The work clears an important milestone on the path

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:01.340
to the plan 2028 launch.

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:04.020
From hardware heading to another planet,

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:07.640
we shift to mapping the outer edges of one much closer to home.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.360
Astronomers have detected an enormous halo of stars

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:14.380
and dark matter surrounding the sombrero galaxy.

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:17.900
The halo extends the known boundaries of the galaxy

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:20.840
and reveals details of its gravitational interactions

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.180
with nearby systems,

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:25.140
quiet evidence of how galaxies continue to grow

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:28.460
through encounters long after their main star-forming days.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:32.760
Large-scale galactic structure gives way to a striking,

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.840
unexpected feature captured much nearer to us.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:38.980
Photographs taken from the Orion spacecraft

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:42.260
during a solar eclipse show a persistent ring of light

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.020
around the moon.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:46.000
The feature remains visible even in regions

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.040
where the moon blocks direct sunlight.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:52.180
And simple camera or atmospheric explanations have been ruled out,

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:54.980
reminding us that even familiar alignments

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:57.120
can still surprise when viewed from orbit.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.680
Space-based eclipse imagery leads us back to ground-based observers

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.900
pushing the limits of what can be captured from suburban skies.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.400
A composite portrait of the pinwheel galaxy

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:13.000
was assembled from 4,173 seconds of exposures

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:17.100
using a small refractor and an unmodified DSLR.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:20.460
The image reveals clear spiral arms

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:23.420
and star-forming regions from dark sky locations

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:25.040
across the American Southwest,

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:28.980
showing what disciplined backyard work can still pull from the dark.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.240
Another amateur success story follows

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:35.400
this time revealing fine detail in a classic nebula.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:38.520
A new image of the elephant's trunk nebula

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:41.200
was created from a 400-minute exposure

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:44.640
that highlights intricate dark lanes and bright emission.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:48.280
The result was attained with compact smart telescopes

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:50.300
operated from suburban sites.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.380
Proof that patient integration time can still uncover structure

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.320
even under light-polluted skies.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:00.300
While amateurs and professionals alike chase photons,

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:04.140
a different kind of cargo recently rode a SpaceX rocket.

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:07.120
Commemorative semi-quinsentennial coins,

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.040
along with matching stamps and NASA mission patches

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:12.520
flew aboard the latest cargo mission to orbit.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:16.620
The items mark America's 250th anniversary

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:19.440
in a symbolic yet routine demonstration

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:21.780
of cultural artifacts traveling to space.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:25.480
Small reminders that exploration carries our stories

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:26.740
along with our instruments.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:29.620
That covers today's Space and Science news.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.020
Share this with a fellow space enthusiast

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.220
if you found it interesting.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:34.880
I'm Patrick and Vancouver.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:35.700
See you tomorrow.

